# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
// Not fixable: without `await`, the code would start with a block.
async function f1() { await {a}.b++; }
const f2 = async () => await {a}.b++;

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-statement-start.js:3:23 lint/nursery/noUselessAwait ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This value is never a promise, so await is unnecessary.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
    2 │ // Not fixable: without `await`, the code would start with a block.
  > 3 │ async function f1() { await {a}.b++; }
      │                       ^^^^^
    4 │ const f2 = async () => await {a}.b++;
    5 │ 
  
  i Awaiting a value that isn't a promise returns the same value, but still delays the code that follows it.
  
  i Remove await. To wait for several promises, pass them to Promise.all() instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

